// PandaBase's additions to the OpenClaw gateway config (README step 11; PLAN M7/M8 Notes).
//
// The gateway can host several agents on one Discord bot, routed by channel and DM sender
// (`bindings`). This file describes PandaBase's side of it: the **`pandabase` agent**, the one
// bound to #pandabase (and the household's other shared channels), which runs PandaBase's
// automations on a local model with no web or browser tools. Other agents on the same gateway
// (e.g. a member's personal agent with web tools and its own Chrome profile) are set up outside
// this repo; they may also have the PandaBase skill and token, but they never drive PandaBase's
// browser. Shared data lives in PandaBase, not in any agent's memory.
//
// Copy to agent/openclaw.pandabase.json5 (gitignored), replace every <…>, then apply:
//
//   openclaw gateway stop
//   openclaw config patch --file agent/openclaw.pandabase.json5 --dry-run   # review the diff
//   openclaw config patch --file agent/openclaw.pandabase.json5
//   openclaw gateway start
//
// Arrays are replaced, not merged: if your config already has `tools.media.models` (e.g. an audio
// transcriber), add these entries to your list by hand. That is also why this patch doesn't touch
// `bindings` or `models.providers.ollama.models` (arrays other agents and onboarding share), nor
// the agents themselves. Set per-agent fields on the agent's own entry, and per-model ones by
// index (OpenClaw 2026.10.10 keeps agents in `agents.entries.<id>`; `agents.list` is rejected):
//
//   # The `pandabase` agent (docs/SETUP-MAC.md §5 step 4; DESIGN §10 #52):
//   openclaw agents add pandabase --non-interactive \
//     --workspace ~/.openclaw/workspace-pandabase --model ollama/<LOCAL_REPLY_MODEL>
//   openclaw config set agents.entries.pandabase.skills \
//     '["digital-receipt-scraper","discord-intake","grocery-cycle","item-lookup","telemetry-aggregator"]' --strict-json
//   openclaw config set agents.entries.pandabase.tools.deny '["group:web","browser"]' --strict-json
//   # plus a `bindings` entry for #pandabase ahead of any catch-all (SETUP-MAC §5 step 4)
//
//   # The VLM's params (README step 11):
//   openclaw config set "models.providers.ollama.models[<i>].params" \
//     '{"num_ctx":8192,"keep_alive":"2m"}' --strict-json
//
// Its id goes in .env as OPENCLAW_AGENT so the automations run as it.
//
// Keep `tools.deny` off the gateway-wide `tools` block below: there it would also take the web
// tools and browser from every other agent on the gateway.
{
  channels: {
    discord: {
      // Needed to read unmentioned messages in #pandabase and in the cycle threads. This Discord
      // policy is gateway-wide: other agents' channels and DMs are configured (and bound) outside
      // this file, and objects merge, so their entries are kept.
      intents: { messageContent: true },
      guilds: {
        "<GUILD_ID>": {
          // A channel map is an allowlist: keep "*" so the bot still answers members when
          // mentioned elsewhere ("do we have eggs?"), but only members. Which agent answers is
          // the gateway's `bindings`' call (by channel and DM sender), not this map's.
          channels: {
            "<PANDABASE_CHANNEL_ID>": {
              enabled: true,
              requireMention: false,
              // Cycle threads are bot-created; follow-ups there shouldn't need a mention.
              requireMentionInBotThreads: false,
              users: ["<MEMBER_1_DISCORD_ID>", "<MEMBER_2_DISCORD_ID>"],
            },
            // `users` is an array: if the gateway already has a "*" rule for other agents'
            // channels, merge the lists by hand rather than let this replace it.
            "*": { requireMention: true, users: ["<MEMBER_1_DISCORD_ID>", "<MEMBER_2_DISCORD_ID>"] },
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },

  // Local vision for inbound photos (PRD §3.6, DESIGN §6): OpenClaw describes each photo with the
  // same Ollama VLM the worker uses, and the reply model gets that text instead of the pixels.
  // Residual risk and the mitigation: README "Photo privacy" (agent/openclaw.privacy.example.json5).
  // Gateway-wide, so it serves every agent's photos. No `deny` here: the `pandabase` agent's
  // web/browser deny is per agent (`agents.entries.pandabase.tools.deny`, header).
  tools: {
    media: {
      models: [
        { provider: "ollama", model: "qwen3.5:9b", capabilities: ["image"], timeoutSeconds: 180 },
      ],
      image: { preferredModel: "ollama/qwen3.5:9b" },
    },
  },

}
